    "aspect": "tall",
    "image": "assets/1000097433.jpg",
    "insight": "Described it as the \"First War of Indian Independence\" and argued that it was a planned national struggle against British rule.\n\nV.D. Savarkar's 1909 landmark text fundamentally reinterpreted the 1857 uprising, shifting the narrative from a mere 'Sepoy Mutiny' to India's first organized war for freedom. \n\nBanned by British authorities prior to publication, it became a major source of ideological inspiration for revolutionary nationalists.",
